lly empty) |\n| 2 | job_id | long | Job identifier |\n| 3 | event_type | int | Type of event (see below) |\n| 4 | user | string | Hashed user identifier |\n| 5 | scheduling_class | int | Scheduling class |\n| 6 | job_name | string | Hashed logical job name |\n| 7 | logical_job_name | string | Hashed logical job name |\n\n## Event Types (shared by both tables)\n\n| Code | Name | Description |\n|------|------|-------------|\n| 0 | SUBMIT | Job/task submitted |\n| 1 | SCHEDULE | Job/task scheduled on a machine |\n| 2 | EVICT | Job/task evicted from machine |\n| 3 | FAIL | Job/task failed |\n| 4 | FINISH | Job/task completed successfully |\n| 5 | KILL | Job/task killed |\n| 6 | LOST | Job/task lost (machine went down) |\n| 7 | UPDATE_PENDING | Update while pending |\n| 8 | UPDATE_RUNNING | Update while running |\n\n## Data Format Notes\n- Files are gzipped CSV (`.csv.gz`)\n- Fields may be empty (consecutive commas)\n- No header row\n- Timestamps are in microseconds (not seconds or milliseconds)\n- 10 minutes = 600,000,000 microseconds\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b4a85629-469b-426f-97ce-dd042cd0d87f"}
{"parentUuid":"f5bcc857-bef1-4c03-8e47-e835af879464","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"53908298-e881-4703-b94d-56576d167fe8","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"humble-whistling-bumblebee","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_013ZAGTNTyrWj268DNnnBHBA","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-streaming-api.md"}]},"uuid":"083464bb-b479-4da6-a151-9d5438b913cc","timestamp":"2026-02-07T05:25:29.672Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-streaming-api.md","content":"# Apache Flink 1.18 Streaming API\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n### StreamExecutionEnvironment\nEntry point for all Flink streaming programs.\n\n```java\nStreamExecutionEnvironment env = StreamExecutionEnvironment.getExecutionEnvironment();\n```\n\n### DataStream API\n- `DataStream<T>` - base stream type\n- `KeyedStream<T, K>` - stream grouped by key\n- `SingleOutputStreamOperator<T>` - result of transformations\n\n### Common Transformations\n```java\n// Map\nstream.map(value -> transform(value));\n\n// FlatMap\nstream.flatMap((value, collector) -> { collector.collect(result); });\n\n// Filter\nstream.filter(value -> condition);\n\n// KeyBy\nstream.keyBy(value -> value.getKey());\n\n// Reduce\nkeyedStream.reduce((v1, v2) -> combine(v1, v2));\n\n// Window\nkeyedStream.window(TumblingEventTimeWindows.of(Time.minutes(5)));\n\n// Process\nkeyedStream.process(new KeyedProcessFunction<K, I, O>() { ... });\n```\n\n### Event Time & Watermarks\n```java\n// Assign timestamps and watermarks\nstream.assignTimestampsAndWatermarks(\n    WatermarkStrategy.<T>forBoundedOutOfOrderness(Duration.ofSeconds(0))\n        .withTimestampAssigner((event, timestamp) -> event.getTimestamp())\n);\n```\n\n### Session Windows\n```java\n// Event-time session windows with a gap\nkeyedStream.window(EventTimeSessionWindows.withGap(Time.minutes(10)))\n    .process(new ProcessWindowFunction<IN, OUT, KEY, TimeWindow>() {\n        @Override\n        public void process(KEY key, Context ctx, Iterable<IN> elements, Collector<OUT> out) {\n            // Process all elements in the session window\n        }\n    });\n```\n\n### Reading from Files\n```java\n// Custom source function for reading gzipped CSV\nenv.addSource(new SourceFunction<T>() { ... });\n\n// Or using readTextFile with custom InputFormat\n```\n\n### Writing to Files\n```java\n// Simple text output\nstream.writeAsText(outputPath, FileSystem.WriteMode.OVERWRITE);\n\n// Or using addSink\nstream.addSink(new SinkFunction<T>() { ... });\n```\n\n### Connected Streams\n```java\n// Connect two streams for co-processing\nDataStream<A> streamA = ...;\nDataStream<B> streamB = ...;\nConnectedStreams<A, B> connected = streamA.connect(streamB);\nconnected.process(new CoProcessFunction<A, B, OUT>() { ... });\n```\n\n## Tuple Types\nFlink provides Tuple types (Tuple2 through Tuple25):\n```java\nimport org.apache.flink.api.java.tuple.Tuple2;\n\nTuple2<Long, Integer> result = Tuple2.of(jobId, count);\n// Access: result.f0, result.f1\n```\n\n## Output Format\nFor `(first_int,second_int)` format:\n```java\nstream.map(tuple -> \"(\" + tuple.f0 + \",\" + tuple.f1 + \")\")\n    .writeAsText(outputPath);\n```\n\n## Parallelism\n```java\nenv.setParallelism(1); // Ensure single output file\n```\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f5bcc857-bef1-4c03-8e47-e835af879464"}
{"parentUuid":"54f1ebb1-2384-429f-8f53-f227d1958899","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"53908298-e881-4703-b94d-56576d167fe8","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"humble-whistling-bumblebee","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01Uv6oBKDdp12L2S99yYQyrT","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-session-window-pattern.md"}]},"uuid":"667c9a7c-7968-4c65-a3ef-d25f20974b89","timestamp":"2026-02-07T05:25:29.686Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-session-window-pattern.md","content":"# Flink Session Window Pattern for Stage Detection\n\n## Problem Pattern\nDetect \"stages\" (bursts of activity separated by inactivity gaps) in a stream of events, grouped by some key.\n\n## Approach: Event-Time Session Windows\n\nSession windows group events that arrive within a specified gap of each other. When no event arrives for the gap duration, the session window closes.\n\n### Implementation\n\n```java\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.windowing.assigners.EventTimeSessionWindows;\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.windowing.time.Time;\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.functions.windowing.ProcessWindowFunction;\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.windowing.windows.TimeWindow;\n\n// Filter to only SUBMIT events, key by jobId, apply session window\ntaskEvents\n    .filter(event -> event.getEventType() == 0) // SUBMIT only\n    .keyBy(event -> event.getJobId())\n    .window(EventTimeSessionWindows.withGap(Time.minutes(10)))\n    .process(new ProcessWindowFunction<TaskEvent, Tuple2<Long, Integer>, Long, TimeWindow>() {\n        @Override\n        public void process(Long jobId, Context ctx, Iterable<TaskEvent> elements, Collector<Tuple2<Long, Integer>> out) {\n            int count = 0;\n            for (TaskEvent e : elements) {\n                count++;\n            }\n            out.collect(Tuple2.of(jobId, count));\n        }\n    });\n```\n\n### Finding the Maximum Stage per Job\nAfter computing stage sizes, find the maximum per job:\n\n```java\nsessionCounts\n    .keyBy(t -> t.f0) // key by jobId\n    .reduce((a, b) -> a.f1 >= b.f1 ? a : b); // keep the one with max count\n```\n\n### Important Considerations\n\n1. **Timestamps**: The dataset uses microseconds. Flink watermarks work with milliseconds. Convert: `timestamp_microseconds / 1000`.\n\n2. **Watermark strategy**: Use `forMonotonousTimestamps()` if data is sorted by time, or `forBoundedOutOfOrderness()` if not.\n\n3. **Gap duration**: 10 minutes = 600 seconds = 600,000 milliseconds.\n\n4. **Only count SUBMIT events** (event_type == 0) for stage detection.\n\n5. **Output only finished jobs**: Join with job events to find jobs that have completed (event_type 4 = FINISH).\n\n## Alternative: KeyedProcessFunction with Timers\n\nFor more control, use `KeyedProcessFunction` with event-time timers:\n\n```java\nkeyedStream.process(new KeyedProcessFunction<Long, TaskEvent, Tuple2<Long, Integer>>() {\n    private ValueState<Integer> currentCount;\n    private ValueState<Long> timerTimestamp;\n    private ValueState<Integer> maxCount;\n\n    @Override\n    public void processElement(TaskEvent event, Context ctx, Collector<Tuple2<Long, Integer>> out) {\n        // Update count, register timer for gap\n        int count = currentCount.value() == null ? 0 : currentCount.value();\n        currentCount.update(count + 1);\n\n        // Clear old timer and set new one\n        Long oldTimer = timerTimestamp.value();\n        if (oldTimer != null) {\n            ctx.timerService().deleteEventTimeTimer(oldTimer);\n        }\n        long newTimer = ctx.timestamp() + 600_000; // 10 minutes in ms\n        ctx.timerService().registerEventTimeTimer(newTimer);\n        timerTimestamp.update(newTimer);\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public void onTimer(long timestamp, OnTimerContext ctx, Collector<Tuple2<Long, Integer>> out) {\n        // Session ended, emit count and track max\n        int count = currentCount.value();\n        int max = maxCount.value() == null ? 0 : maxCount.value();\n        maxCount.update(Math.max(max, count));\n        currentCount.update(0);\n    }\n});\n```\n\n## Combining with Job Finish Events\nTo only output results for finished jobs, connect the task event stream with the job event stream:\n\n```java\n// Method 1: CoProcessFunction on connected streams\ntaskResults.connect(finishedJobs)\n    .keyBy(t -> t.f0, j -> j.getJobId())\n    .process(new CoProcessFunction<...>() { ... });\n\n// Method 2: Process all data in batch-style, then filter\n```\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"54f1ebb1-2384-429f-8f53-f227d1958899"}
{"parentUuid":"1d8c926b-03a6-44df-a991-09fde07d6d82","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"53908298-e881-4703-b94d-56576d167fe8","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"humble-whistling-bumblebee","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01FNtavNKkUSEQ32yZHhd9TP","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-gzip-csv-source.md"}]},"uuid":"d21f9d3c-d6c3-476e-9e52-57692cd8b158","timestamp":"2026-02-07T05:25:29.699Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-gzip-csv-source.md","content":"# Reading Gzipped CSV Files in Flink\n\n## Approach: Custom SourceFunction\n\nFlink can read gzipped files using `GZIPInputStream`. Create a custom `SourceFunction` to parse CSV lines.\n\n### Implementation Pattern\n\n```java\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.functions.source.SourceFunction;\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.zip.GZIPInputStream;\n\npublic class TaskEventSource implements SourceFunction<TaskEvent> {\n    private final String filePath;\n    private volatile boolean running = true;\n\n    public TaskEventSource(String filePath) {\n        this.filePath = filePath;\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public void run(SourceContext<TaskEvent> ctx) throws Exception {\n        try (BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(\n                new InputStreamReader(new GZIPInputStream(new FileInputStream(filePath))))) {\n            String line;\n            while (running && (line = reader.readLine()) != null) {\n                TaskEvent event = TaskEvent.fromCsv(line);\n                if (event != null) {\n                    ctx.collect(event);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public void cancel() {\n        running = false;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Alternative: Flink Built-in TextInputFormat\n\n```java\n// Flink can handle .gz files natively with readTextFile\nDataStream<String> lines = env.readTextFile(inputPath);\n\n// Then parse each line\nDataStream<TaskEvent> events = lines.map(line -> TaskEvent.fromCsv(line));\n```\n\n**Note**: `readTextFile` in Flink automatically handles `.gz` files if the path ends with `.gz`. However, gzip files are not splittable, so they'll be read by a single reader.\n\n### CSV Parsing for Empty Fields\n\nThe Google cluster data CSVs have empty fields (consecutive commas). Use careful parsing:\n\n```java\npublic static TaskEvent fromCsv(String line) {\n    String[] parts = line.split(\",\", -1); // -1 to keep trailing empty strings\n    // parts[i] may be \"\" for empty fields\n    long timestamp = parts[0].isEmpty() ? 0 : Long.parseLong(parts[0]);\n    // ... etc\n}\n```\n\n### Important Notes\n- Always use `split(\",\", -1)` to preserve empty trailing fields\n- Check for empty strings before parsing numeric fields\n- Gzipped files can't be split across parallel readers\n- Set parallelism to 1 for file reading or handle in source\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1d8c926b-03a6-44df-a991-09fde07d6d82"}
{"parentUuid":"e5db9696-8c8e-45ce-a965-87459ee6547a","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"53908298-e881-4703-b94d-56576d167fe8","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"humble-whistling-bumblebee","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01MZWiPkVNSryDRjrcceZfnA","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-data-types-pojo.md"}]},"uuid":"9578f936-bf01-4301-85af-853c52c61086","timestamp":"2026-02-07T05:25:29.712Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-data-types-pojo.md","content":"# Flink Data Types and POJOs\n\n## POJO Requirements for Flink\n\nFor Flink to efficiently serialize a class as a POJO:\n1. The class must be public and standalone (no non-static inner class)\n2. The class must have a public no-argument constructor\n3. All fields must be public OR have public getters/setters\n4. All field types must be supported by Flink's type system\n\n### Example POJO\n\n```java\npackage clusterdata.datatypes;\n\nimport java.io.Serializable;\n\npublic class TaskEvent implements Serializable {\n    public long timestamp;\n    public String missingInfo;\n    public long jobId;\n    public int taskIndex;\n    public long machineId;\n    public int eventType;\n    public String user;\n    public int schedulingClass;\n    public int priority;\n    public double cpuRequest;\n    public double memoryRequest;\n    public double diskRequest;\n    public int constraint;\n\n    // Required no-arg constructor\n    public TaskEvent() {}\n\n    // Constructor with fields\n    public TaskEvent(long timestamp, long jobId, int taskIndex, int eventType) {\n        this.timestamp = timestamp;\n        this.jobId = jobId;\n        this.taskIndex = taskIndex;\n        this.eventType = eventType;\n    }\n\n    // Factory method for CSV parsing\n    public static TaskEvent fromCsv(String line) {\n        String[] parts = line.split(\",\", -1);\n        TaskEvent event = new TaskEvent();\n        event.timestamp = parts[0].isEmpty() ? 0L : Long.parseLong(parts[0]);\n        event.missingInfo = parts[1];\n        event.jobId = parts[2].isEmpty() ? 0L : Long.parseLong(parts[2]);\n        event.taskIndex = parts[3].isEmpty() ? 0 : Integer.parseInt(parts[3]);\n        event.machineId = parts[4].isEmpty() ? -1L : Long.parseLong(parts[4]);\n        event.eventType = parts[5].isEmpty() ? -1 : Integer.parseInt(parts[5]);\n        event.user = parts[6];\n        event.schedulingClass = parts[7].isEmpty() ? 0 : Integer.parseInt(parts[7]);\n        event.priority = parts[8].isEmpty() ? 0 : Integer.parseInt(parts[8]);\n        event.cpuRequest = parts[9].isEmpty() ? 0.0 : Double.parseDouble(parts[9]);\n        event.memoryRequest = parts[10].isEmpty() ? 0.0 : Double.parseDouble(parts[10]);\n        event.diskRequest = parts[11].isEmpty() ? 0.0 : Double.parseDouble(parts[11]);\n        event.constraint = parts[12].isEmpty() ? 0 : Integer.parseInt(parts[12]);\n        return event;\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public String toString() {\n        return \"TaskEvent{\" +\n            \"timestamp=\" + timestamp +\n            \", jobId=\" + jobId +\n            \", taskIndex=\" + taskIndex +\n            \", eventType=\" + eventType +\n            '}';\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Event Type Constants\n\n```java\npublic static final int SUBMIT = 0;\npublic static final int SCHEDULE = 1;\npublic static final int EVICT = 2;\npublic static final int FAIL = 3;\npublic static final int FINISH = 4;\npublic static final int KILL = 5;\npublic static final int LOST = 6;\npublic static final int UPDATE_PENDING = 7;\npublic static final int UPDATE_RUNNING = 8;\n```\n\n## Flink Tuple Types\n\nFor simple output, use Flink's built-in Tuple types:\n```java\nimport org.apache.flink.api.java.tuple.Tuple2;\n\nTuple2<Long, Integer> result = Tuple2.of(123L, 45);\n// result.f0 = 123L (jobId)\n// result.f1 = 45 (count)\n```\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e5db9696-8c8e-45ce-a965-87459ee6547a"}
